WEBVTT

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:06.650
<b>GUNDAM
VICTORY
MOBILE SUIT</b>

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:12.610
The furious rain, Makes my heart shake
hageshii ame ga, kokoro wo yuruwaseru

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:15.820
Like it did on that day
Ano hi no youni

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:22.910
But I just ran through, In my dream I had till yesterday
Tada hashirinuketa, kinou made no MY DREAM

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.710
...I still believe
...shinjiteiru no sa

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:34.470
I'm willing to fight, An endless defense
Owari no nai, defense demo ii yo

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:42.350
As long as you, Keep on gazing at me
Kimi ga boku wo, mitsumetsuzukete kureru nara

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:45.270
STAND UP TO THE VICTORY!

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.980
Turn to face all the mornings ahead, And someday
Ikutsumono asa wo mukae, Itsuka kitto

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:53.860
Try to seize them
tsukande miseru

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:56.450
STAND UP TO THE VICTORY!

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:02.120
Even if nothing, Lies on the other side
Sono mukougawa ni, nanimonakutemo

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:06.040
It doesn't matter to me
kamawanai kara

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:14.050
...Just as long as I can embrace, Your gentle, irreplaceable smile!
Kakegae no nai, kimi no yasashii egao daite

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:24.530
Shahkti!

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:25.960
You can't stay here!

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:27.060
Üso!

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:31.060
In the battle at Bechyne,

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.560
Helen of Shrike Team died in combat.

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:39.830
In battle, a moment of stubbornness will cost you your life.

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:47.400
Üso learned that harsh lesson,

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:50.500
shortly after being told they were headed south.

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:55.100
Üso wept until he could weep no more.

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:06.730
Gomez's transport team tried to head west, but found their course blocked.

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:09.160
SMASH THE GUILLOTINE

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:11.260
"Smash The Guillotine"!
SMASH THE GUILLOTINE

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:11.960
SMASH THE GUILLOTINE

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:27.630
Dammit, have the kid get further away from us!

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:32.600
God, he keeps flying for Arti Gibraltar without thinking!

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:36.860
He's taking that course by flying along the clouds, right?

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:40.500
Incoming! Two contacts, bearing 3 o'clock!

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:44.800
I guess we can't slip through Largaine's net.

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:47.800
I've got an alarm! Tell Shrike Team to hide their mobile suits!

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:50.700
We've been spotted?

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:56.900
Two enemy units from the northwest. Two scout planes.

00:02:56.930 --> 00:03:00.860
This is the BESPA Yellow Jackets. Come in! Please come in!

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:08.400
This is the BESPA Yellow Jackets! Please come in!

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:13.160
This is PCST transport, en-route to Arti Gibraltar.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.900
You're not on the corporate route!

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:18.460
I wish to confirm. Please ascend out of the clouds.

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:22.460
It's beat-up old plane. I'll get her out if I can.

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:23.300
Well?

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:26.800
We're moving two of the Shrike Team to act as our engines.

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:32.300
Cony, once you're hooked on the left side, you can ease off the thrust.

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:42.060
Okay!

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:43.930
Out we go!

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:55.430
It's embarrassing how lopsided this old junkheap flies.

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:59.100
Where's your third plane? Transports don't fly in wings of two.

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:02.000
What, I have a third plane? Where is it?

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:06.660
Can you hear me on the closed circuit, Lt. Gomez?

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:08.760
I'll wait for you in the next port town.

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:11.300
We're just a two plane wing here.

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:15.600
I see now! We're being followed!

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:17.460
It's really close! What's going on?!

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:26.500
Is that a part of that white mobile suit?

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:32.800
Oh, no! It's a League Militaire mobile suit!

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:35.630
Is it attacking our totally neutral company?!

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:41.200
Damn PCST! They got followed by rats?

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:42.200
There it is!

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:46.130
Good, they fell for it.

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:51.660
Just once more!

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:54.860
Was that Üso?

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:56.530
Üso, that was too close!

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:03.560
He's gone? How can a 14 or 15 year old kid do stuff like that?

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:07.060
He's more pilot than child, without a doubt.

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:08.360
So it would seem.

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:11.960
He's given your resistance movement some motivation, huh?

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:15.030
He's definitely given us confidence.

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:20.560
It's often said that children's intuition is usually right.

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:24.200
No chance of breaking through to Ireland, huh?

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:28.130
Getting to Arti Gibraltar may be the bigger question.

00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:39.230
They're really hanging in there.

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:48.000
He's out of ammo, too! Dammit, and we finally caught up!

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:53.230
I'll drive them off!

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:04.960
Nice job.

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:24.360
This is the sea?

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:26.360
It's amazing!

00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:31.100
So, this is the ocean.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:16.500
What's that?

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:35.260
What's with all this garbage?

00:07:42.830 --> 00:07:44.360
There's some really old stuff in here.

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:45.530
Thief!

00:07:46.130 --> 00:07:49.300
Did you come to steal a man's hard-earned collection?!

00:07:49.600 --> 00:07:51.960
You collected this, sir?

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:54.330
Nichol!

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:56.900
No... Who are you?

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:12.600
A fish reef? You use that to make a place for fish to live?

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:15.630
Yeah. When you sink mobile suit panels into the sea,

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:18.400
the fish like to concentrate around them.

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:20.360
Didn't I teach you that, Nichol?

00:08:21.130 --> 00:08:24.900
Uh, you only taught me how to drive a boat.

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:30.130
We can make it work! Just line up the induction fans.

00:08:31.230 --> 00:08:34.460
Odelo! Bring those parts I wanted over here.

00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:36.930
I am! She wants us to hurry.

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:38.000
This one?

00:08:38.130 --> 00:08:38.830
Yeah.

00:08:39.630 --> 00:08:42.800
If we head into the port, we can get some information.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:43.830
I guess, but...

00:08:43.860 --> 00:08:47.230
If it's a big town, maybe we can buy some sweets, too.

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:47.830
Well?

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:49.560
Scout the perimeter, huh?

00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:50.630
Okay, then!

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:53.530
Where are you going?

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:56.000
We need to find something good to eat!

00:08:57.230 --> 00:09:00.460
Shahkti's going scouting, too? What's going on?

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:08.200
Now that Earth's been dragged into another space war,

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:11.700
I can't do my research or fish, either, Nichol.

00:09:12.060 --> 00:09:12.800
Right...

00:09:17.900 --> 00:09:20.130
Coming with me to the market, Nichol?

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:21.860
It's Üso Ewin.

00:09:23.130 --> 00:09:25.060
Oh, dear. I'm going senile.

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:29.560
The library's right around that corner.

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:30.930
Thank you, Mr. Rob!

00:09:31.060 --> 00:09:32.700
Come to my place for supper.

00:09:32.730 --> 00:09:33.430
Sure thing.

00:09:38.630 --> 00:09:39.660
Nichol, huh?

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:44.100
Dammit, we were one step away.

00:09:44.900 --> 00:09:46.900
Besides that, there's Commander Fuala.

00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:50.500
She's become more of a hard ass since the guillotine incident.

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:55.200
Hey, lady! Wanna have some fun!

00:09:55.230 --> 00:09:56.360
No! Stop!

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:57.760
Huh? Why?

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:02.430
Don't tell me...

00:10:02.530 --> 00:10:04.500
It certainly is...

00:10:06.630 --> 00:10:08.930
203rd reconnaissance group...

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:10.460
Reporting, ma'am! Reporting, ma'am!

00:10:11.300 --> 00:10:13.400
Carry on. Understood?

00:10:13.430 --> 00:10:14.100
Yes, ma'am!

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:19.760
I can breathe again.

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:29.460
This place is great.

00:10:29.530 --> 00:10:32.360
Yeah, there are still houses you can live in.

00:10:32.660 --> 00:10:35.030
I'm going where Üso is.

00:10:35.330 --> 00:10:36.530
Where is he?

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:38.630
Where there are lots of books.

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:43.330
Are there people camping out in here?

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:44.500
Sure.

00:10:44.530 --> 00:10:45.630
Flanders?

00:10:53.430 --> 00:10:54.800
Oh! Flanders!

00:10:54.830 --> 00:10:55.460
See?

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:57.360
Hi! What are you researching now?

00:10:57.960 --> 00:11:00.300
A course to Arti Gibraltar.

00:11:00.330 --> 00:11:02.360
Come on, let's go back to Kasarelia.

00:11:02.400 --> 00:11:03.300
Yeah!

00:11:04.630 --> 00:11:05.660
Live here?

00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:09.800
Yeah. Seems like a nice spot. We could do well here.

00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:13.430
Check this out! The fridge on the second floor's amazing!

00:11:13.460 --> 00:11:14.500
It's full of canned goods!

00:11:14.530 --> 00:11:15.830
All right, jackpot!

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:17.600
Suzy!

00:11:18.130 --> 00:11:19.160
It's Sis!

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:21.300
Sis?

00:11:21.330 --> 00:11:23.330
She wouldn't be here.

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:24.330
What's up?

00:11:27.360 --> 00:11:29.230
Sister!

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:37.060
I-I'm sorry! I thought you were someone else.

00:11:37.100 --> 00:11:39.700
I'm sorry, she's a war orphan, so...

00:11:40.360 --> 00:11:44.700
I look like your sister? There's a lot of you, huh?

00:11:45.530 --> 00:11:47.930
We were thinking of trying to find a place to live around here.

00:11:47.960 --> 00:11:52.630
I see. It's nice to have friends to live with.

00:11:52.860 --> 00:11:56.060
But this city wouldn't be a good place for that.

00:11:56.600 --> 00:11:59.600
I see. Is it being targeted by BESPA?

00:11:59.830 --> 00:12:01.260
Be careful.

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:07.930
There are people in there. Lots of them.

00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:08.760
Yeah.

00:12:27.330 --> 00:12:28.160
Beer.

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:29.600
And for her?

00:12:32.300 --> 00:12:34.300
Would you like some chocolate?

00:12:34.330 --> 00:12:35.100
Yes!

00:12:35.260 --> 00:12:36.100
You have any?

00:12:36.130 --> 00:12:37.030
Yes.

00:12:37.130 --> 00:12:38.600
They have chocolate!

00:12:44.960 --> 00:12:46.900
BESPA military scrip?

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:48.000
Problem?

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:50.530
Please finish your drink and then leave!

00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:53.130
Is it good?

00:12:55.200 --> 00:12:56.360
Get lost!

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:57.930
I'm sorry.

00:12:59.260 --> 00:13:00.260
They're scared.

00:13:02.030 --> 00:13:03.100
The south airport?

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:04.660
It's occupied by BESPA.

00:13:05.630 --> 00:13:06.430
BESPA?

00:13:06.600 --> 00:13:11.230
Üso, use this to buy something soft for Karl.

00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:13.130
Sure. Wait here.

00:13:16.300 --> 00:13:17.560
Isn't it amazing?

00:13:25.860 --> 00:13:27.560
Orders from Pippiniden?

00:13:27.600 --> 00:13:32.160
No. There's a request to display the guillotine here.

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:34.360
A "request," what nonsense!

00:13:34.400 --> 00:13:36.160
Are you traveling, Miss?

00:13:37.400 --> 00:13:38.530
Sort of.

00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:41.600
Pardon, do you have warm milk?

00:13:43.730 --> 00:13:45.560
I'll take that for these two, as well.

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:46.360
Huh?

00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:49.830
We can't all sponge off people we meet for the first time.

00:13:49.900 --> 00:13:50.560
Right?

00:13:51.230 --> 00:13:52.460
If only we could.

00:13:52.630 --> 00:13:53.860
This is Üso.

00:13:53.900 --> 00:13:57.160
He can be a little timid, but he's thoughtful and easygoing.

00:13:59.030 --> 00:13:59.960
It's a pleasure.

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:01.830
F-For me, too!

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:03.700
I have an idea.

00:14:03.930 --> 00:14:06.560
In every area where the League Militaire are gathering,

00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:09.860
we threaten the general populace with a symbol on Zanscare.

00:14:09.900 --> 00:14:12.800
Let it be your show, then. You set up the guillotines.

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:13.960
I will.

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:19.060
Must my history with the guillotine follow me around?

00:14:20.100 --> 00:14:22.430
Are you a war orphan too, ma'am?

00:14:23.100 --> 00:14:24.960
I never had a home.

00:14:27.160 --> 00:14:29.360
Okay, just sit it down there.

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:31.460
Good!

00:14:31.530 --> 00:14:33.460
Junko, get some rest!

00:14:33.660 --> 00:14:35.100
Üso's still advancing, right?

00:14:35.130 --> 00:14:38.030
You don't need to worry about him. He's that sort of kid.

00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:41.300
Shrike Team was originally the main unit of the League Militaire!

00:14:41.330 --> 00:14:43.330
I don't want to let that kid just do everything!

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:46.430
Mahalia! Hurry up!

00:14:47.360 --> 00:14:48.760
They just had hot milk.

00:14:48.960 --> 00:14:49.900
It's fine.

00:14:53.430 --> 00:14:54.300
It's BESPA!

00:14:54.560 --> 00:14:55.330
BESPA?

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:57.100
Just act natural.

00:14:57.330 --> 00:14:58.000
Right.

00:15:03.230 --> 00:15:04.160
A guillotine?

00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:06.730
It's BESPA! They've brought out the guillotine!

00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:08.260
They said they're putting it in the main square!

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:09.800
Who's going to the guillotine?!

00:15:09.830 --> 00:15:11.830
Are they kidding? This is a free city!

00:15:11.860 --> 00:15:14.630
Looks like BESPA wants to expand their sphere of influence.

00:15:14.660 --> 00:15:16.960
Get out, BESPA! This isn't Zanscare!

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:19.200
How can they set it up in front of my place?

00:15:22.660 --> 00:15:24.700
Screw you people! Don't execute anyone here!

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:25.800
Get out, Zanscare!

00:15:25.830 --> 00:15:27.600
We don't want this here!

00:15:27.630 --> 00:15:29.260
Go back to space, Zanscare!

00:15:29.300 --> 00:15:30.600
Don't pollute the Earth!

00:15:30.630 --> 00:15:31.900
Down with BESPA!

00:15:31.930 --> 00:15:35.060
It would have been better to have nothing in this square!

00:15:35.600 --> 00:15:38.130
We're not executing anyone here. We're just setting it here.

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:40.130
We don't want any Zanscare soldiers here!

00:15:40.160 --> 00:15:42.260
The guillotine is... Who did that?!

00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:46.160
This town doesn't need this awful thing! Leave!

00:15:47.860 --> 00:15:48.760
I don't believe this!

00:15:48.900 --> 00:15:49.860
It's for real!

00:15:49.900 --> 00:15:51.130
They used the guillotine!

00:15:51.160 --> 00:15:52.700
Someone stop them!

00:15:52.900 --> 00:15:55.530
Are you going to shoot unarmed people?!

00:15:56.460 --> 00:15:57.600
It's Mr. Rob's voice!

00:15:57.660 --> 00:15:58.530
You know him?

00:15:58.800 --> 00:16:00.500
Everybody, get back to the transport!

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:01.830
See you!

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:05.930
Stop it!

00:16:06.060 --> 00:16:07.660
Go back to space!

00:16:07.700 --> 00:16:08.760
Stop, please!

00:16:09.930 --> 00:16:10.900
Why, you!

00:16:11.660 --> 00:16:15.360
Anyone who insults the guillotine of Zanscare will be shot!

00:16:16.130 --> 00:16:17.300
Damn you!

00:16:21.100 --> 00:16:22.430
Nichol, don't run!

00:16:22.460 --> 00:16:24.430
You can't take on soldiers like that!

00:16:24.860 --> 00:16:27.830
Arrest the fisherman who started the riot!

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:29.700
Okay!

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:30.730
Üso!

00:16:32.530 --> 00:16:37.530
But, I won't forgive an army that took you away for war!

00:16:42.760 --> 00:16:45.630
Will they do anything just to make you go to war?

00:16:45.660 --> 00:16:46.500
Now what?

00:16:46.530 --> 00:16:49.400
You won't die today! I won't let you die!

00:16:49.430 --> 00:16:50.330
Mr. Rob?

00:17:07.760 --> 00:17:08.900
Okay, Üso?

00:17:08.930 --> 00:17:10.860
Rendezvous with the transport over the ocean!

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:13.100
We'll have Shrike Team run interference for you!

00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:16.260
I understand! I'll be fine.

00:17:16.400 --> 00:17:18.800
Don't try anything on your own.

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:19.960
I know.

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:30.530
I'm not Nichol... I'm Üso!

00:17:40.630 --> 00:17:42.330
Kwan Lee's team?

00:17:42.360 --> 00:17:43.500
That's going a bit far.

00:17:44.260 --> 00:17:45.530
And the Recarl?

00:17:48.060 --> 00:17:49.760
It's not just the riot in the city!

00:17:49.800 --> 00:17:53.360
We've picked up possible League Militaire mobile suit movement!

00:17:54.960 --> 00:17:56.730
Has the white one appeared?

00:17:57.130 --> 00:17:57.860
Yes, ma'am!

00:17:59.960 --> 00:18:03.030
Mr. Rob... I'm going to smash that guillotine!

00:18:13.100 --> 00:18:13.900
There!

00:18:16.030 --> 00:18:17.160
Why, you!

00:18:22.030 --> 00:18:23.230
It's the League Militaire!

00:18:26.560 --> 00:18:27.530
I got it!

00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:34.760
Minovsky particle oscillation and chaff!

00:18:45.400 --> 00:18:48.500
They've stationed three mobile suits at this airport?

00:18:49.660 --> 00:18:52.930
I thought it was the Gundam replica, but it's just part of it?

00:18:53.130 --> 00:18:54.100
In that case...

00:18:55.530 --> 00:18:56.130
What?

00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:01.460
Where'd that attack come from?

00:19:09.200 --> 00:19:10.030
They're fast!

00:19:11.360 --> 00:19:14.200
You've got good teamwork, but I won't let you hit me!

00:19:15.360 --> 00:19:18.360
This is the formation we learned from Pippiniden!

00:19:21.500 --> 00:19:24.300
The ones the base picked up are that way?

00:19:24.530 --> 00:19:26.160
The machine over the city!

00:19:26.200 --> 00:19:27.630
It was a decoy?

00:19:29.130 --> 00:19:31.230
Üso, rendezvous with Shrike Team!

00:19:34.030 --> 00:19:37.830
With Miss Marbet and Mr. Oliver here, I can win!

00:19:39.500 --> 00:19:40.560
Shield!

00:19:43.930 --> 00:19:45.060
Saber!

00:19:53.360 --> 00:19:54.130
What?

00:20:02.760 --> 00:20:03.800
Next?

00:20:04.630 --> 00:20:05.460
Here he comes!

00:20:09.760 --> 00:20:11.630
You want me to get in formation?

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:18.260
Kwan Lee is heavily damaged?

00:20:18.300 --> 00:20:21.200
But he's managed to escape the combat airspace.

00:20:21.230 --> 00:20:24.160
We count three League Militaire units. Here they come!

00:20:24.930 --> 00:20:28.000
Can't I drink one beer in a pub without trouble?

00:20:31.030 --> 00:20:33.400
One? Aren't there three?

00:20:33.430 --> 00:20:36.800
It's three, but with radar knocked out, I can't tell!

00:20:37.460 --> 00:20:39.930
Is it a single-line formation, or some other trick?

00:20:40.760 --> 00:20:43.360
Suppressing fire! Break their formation!

00:20:47.200 --> 00:20:48.060
Die!

00:20:51.600 --> 00:20:53.400
Metchet, shoot them down!

00:20:58.300 --> 00:20:59.730
You think that'll kill me?!

00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:05.860
The cannon barrel has been destroyed!

00:21:05.900 --> 00:21:08.360
We still have the beam rifles and vulcans!

00:21:08.400 --> 00:21:11.100
Our main engine is also in danger of exploding!

00:21:11.730 --> 00:21:12.900
Will we self-destruct?

00:21:13.260 --> 00:21:17.900
No... If you order it, I'll stay in pursuit! We're all right!

00:21:18.330 --> 00:21:19.260
I see!

00:21:19.300 --> 00:21:20.060
Yes, ma'am!

00:21:20.800 --> 00:21:21.930
Pursuing!

00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:23.730
No. There's no point.

00:21:23.760 --> 00:21:25.000
Yes, ma'am!

00:21:28.030 --> 00:21:31.800
Metchet, you're a good man.

00:21:32.630 --> 00:21:36.360
Üso, do you read? I don't know what happened on the ground, but...

00:21:36.400 --> 00:21:37.530
Commander Oliver?

00:21:38.060 --> 00:21:40.400
Üso knows, without you needing to say it.

00:21:40.800 --> 00:21:45.300
He was able to handle that formation battle with no explanation.

00:21:45.430 --> 00:21:46.560
Miss Marbet...

00:21:46.800 --> 00:21:48.660
Thanks to this air battle,

00:21:48.700 --> 00:21:51.400
Lt. Gomez has started making his way south.

00:21:52.660 --> 00:21:54.530
That's thanks to you too, Üso.

00:21:55.260 --> 00:21:56.360
Good job.

00:22:24.060 --> 00:22:29.530
Piercing the sky, Blue lightning
sora wo tsukisasu aoi inazuma

00:22:29.530 --> 00:22:35.320
Staining the earth, With the shadow of greed
daichi o someteku, yokubou no kage

00:22:36.370 --> 00:22:41.460
Once again, when the nightmare, Envelops the Earth
futatabi akumu ga, sekai wo tsutsumu toki

00:22:41.460 --> 00:22:46.790
You hear voices crying out "S.O.S."
"SOS" wo sakebu koe ga kikoeru...

00:22:48.630 --> 00:22:54.130
Let proud hope fill your heart
hokoritakaki kibou wo mune ni

00:22:54.720 --> 00:23:03.100
And stand up! Say a prayer for peace!!
tachiagare! heiwa no inori komete!

00:23:04.100 --> 00:23:05.100
WINNERS FOREVER!

00:23:06.100 --> 00:23:08.980
In every age
itsuno jidai mo

00:23:08.980 --> 00:23:14.570
...People take risks for freedom
hito wa jiyuu wo kakete

00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:17.000
WINNERS FOREVER!

00:23:18.330 --> 00:23:21.240
The battle goes on
tatakai tsuzukeru

00:23:21.240 --> 00:23:25.920
Fighting all alone in solitude
kodoku na made ni hitori...

00:23:33.200 --> 00:23:37.530
Going to Arti Gibraltar to ask about his parents,

00:23:38.300 --> 00:23:41.330
Üso once again meets the lady from the pub.

00:23:42.260 --> 00:23:45.030
And because he's fighting Fuala's machine,

00:23:45.530 --> 00:23:49.260
Üso is unable to protect Mahalia.

00:23:50.600 --> 00:23:53.330
Next time, on Mobile Suit Victory Gundam:

00:23:54.200 --> 00:23:54.360
"Gibraltar Airspace".

00:23:54.360 --> 00:23:56.660
Next Episode GIBRALTAR AIRSPACE

00:23:56.660 --> 00:23:57.760
Please watch it!

00:23:57.760 --> 00:23:59.300
Next Episode GIBRALTAR AIRSPACE
